    "scene_specificity": {
      "total": 11,
      "specific_count": 9,
      "ratio": 0.818,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "s01",
          "role": "hook",
          "est_duration_s": 5.5,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:DGX Spark"
          ],
          "narration": "Your DGX Spark just hit its ceiling. The newest open models grew past what your box can hold."
        },
        {
          "id": "s02",
          "role": "foreshadow",
          "est_duration_s": 12.4,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:753B params",
            "entity:GLM"
          ],
          "narration": "An open model called GLM five point two just landed. Its card lists seven hundred fifty-three billion parameters, the stored dials a model reads to write. No single graphics card you can buy holds them all."
        },
        {
          "id": "s03",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 9.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:unified memory"
          ],
          "narration": "Your Spark carries one hundred twenty-eight gigabytes of unified memory, one pool the processor and the graphics chip share. That was roomy last year. This model is roomier."
        },
        {
          "id": "s04",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:512 GB",
            "entity:Sparks"
          ],
          "narration": "So you cable four Sparks together. Tensor parallelism, the trick that splits one model across boxes, pools their memory into one heap. Four boxes give five hundred twelve gigabytes of pooled memory, and the giant finally fits."
        },
        {
          "id": "s05",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 10.5,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Petronella"
          ],
          "narration": "Here is the catch, straight from Petronella's measurements. Inside a box, memory feeds the chip over a wide road. The cable between boxes is about a tenth as wide. Every word pulls some weights through it."
        },
        {
          "id": "s06",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 6.8,
          "specific": false,
          "hits": [],
          "narration": "Picture four movers with one piano. Together they lift it, but they keep stopping to call out the next step."
        },
        {
          "id": "s07",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.5,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:26.5 tok/s",
            "entity:GLM",
            "entity:Petronella"
          ],
          "narration": "A benchmark team called Petronella ran four boxes on GLM five point three Flash, a smaller open model. On plain prose it decoded twenty-six point five tokens per second. A token is a chunk of a word, so that is reading pace."
        },
        {
          "id": "s08",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 7.5,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Qwen"
          ],
          "narration": "The piano picture bends for sparse models like Qwen three point eight Flash Next, a kind that wakes only a few small specialists per word. There, more boxes really do pay."
        },
        {
          "id": "s09",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Ellis",
            "entity:Sparks",
            "entity:Alex Ellis"
          ],
          "narration": "Alex Ellis's team built this. They cabled four Sparks into a closed ring, with no network switch at all. They also patched the networking library that moves data between boxes, so neighbors relay."
        },
        {
          "id": "s10",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 9.0,
          "specific": false,
          "hits": [],
          "narration": "So what did four boxes buy? Not speed. The decode strolls at reading pace. They bought a model class your shelf could not hold yesterday."
        },
        {
          "id": "s11",
          "role": "payoff_close",
          "est_duration_s": 8.6,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Sparks"
          ],
          "narration": "Four Sparks buy memory, not speed. The model that outgrew your one box now fits on four, and it answers at the pace you read."
        }
      ]
    },
